1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,673
ResearchAgent: research with a
wallet on XRPL Testnet.

2
00:00:03,673 --> 00:00:04,927
Paid on delivery.

3
00:00:04,927 --> 00:00:06,400
Proven on the ledger.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,772
The featured recorded run is from 12
November: all five gates held.

5
00:00:12,772 --> 00:00:15,288
Verify it without asking a question.

6
00:00:15,288 --> 00:00:19,600
The browser reports twenty-four checks
passed and two not checked.

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:32,749
How does the writer get paid, and what
stops the agent from reading the article

8
00:00:32,749 --> 00:00:35,065
and then refusing to pay?

9
00:00:35,065 --> 00:00:36,484
Set a budget.

10
00:00:36,484 --> 00:00:37,754
40 article.

11
00:00:37,754 --> 00:00:39,846
Only policy code pays.

12
00:00:39,846 --> 00:00:46,569
The key that unlocks the article is the same key
that releases the writer's payment.

13
00:00:46,569 --> 00:00:51,200
Show work compares the searches
with the confirmed plan.

14
00:00:59,789 --> 00:01:03,117
The writer collects by publishing the article key.

15
00:01:03,117 --> 00:01:06,742
Signed submission can expose the
key before validation.

16
00:01:06,742 --> 00:01:11,794
This browser reads the create and finish from
a public node and hashes the key.

17
00:01:11,794 --> 00:01:12,804
It matches.

18
00:01:12,804 --> 00:01:15,538
That proves the key reveal, not quality.

19
00:01:15,538 --> 00:01:20,589
This recorded refund needed the writer's
signature; a real writer could refuse.

20
00:01:21,789 --> 00:01:25,493
Claude Code can use the same
research tools over MCP.

21
00:01:25,493 --> 00:01:30,892
The spending caps come from the environment;
the calling model can't raise them.

22
00:01:30,892 --> 00:01:35,789
This result cites our own labelled notes
and links its Testnet payments.

23
00:01:39,789 --> 00:01:42,964
Export the receipts and check them outside the app.

24
00:01:42,964 --> 00:01:46,640
Our TypeScript and Python verifiers
were written separately.

25
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:52,154
Read the passed and skipped checks; a receipt
verification result does not certify a writer's

26
00:01:52,154 --> 00:01:52,989
identity.

27
00:01:54,089 --> 00:01:57,653
Three operator-run writers now hold
accepted Testnet Credentials.

28
00:01:57,653 --> 00:02:02,823
A Testnet Permissioned Domain lists the credential
issuer and type accepted for identity display.

29
00:02:02,823 --> 00:02:06,889
It's our attestation: not KYC, quality
certification or payment permission.

30
00:02:07,989 --> 00:02:09,912
We ask rippled before signing.

31
00:02:09,912 --> 00:02:14,933
In recorded unsigned probes, RLUSD escrow returned
no permission on Testnet and Mainnet.

32
00:02:14,933 --> 00:02:17,924
The matched TEST-SGD control succeeded on Testnet.

33
00:02:17,924 --> 00:02:19,419
Nothing was submitted.

34
00:02:19,419 --> 00:02:24,280
Our browser sandbox pays in Testnet XRP;
TEST-SGD is a labelled stand-in, and mainnet

35
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,989
spending remains disabled.

36
00:02:30,989 --> 00:02:34,050
Check the recorded proof, then ask your question.

37
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:37,389
ResearchAgent: paid on delivery,
